.TH RBINKD 8 "19 Nov 2026"
.SH NAME
rbinkd \- Rust reimplementation of the Binkd Fidonet mailer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rbinkd
.RB [ \-CcDipqrsvdmh ]
.RB [
.B \-P
.I node
]
.I config-file
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rbinkd
is a Rust reimplementation of the Binkd Fidonet mailer. It transfers FTN
mail and files over TCP/IP with the binkp protocol.
.PP
On supported platforms,
.B rbinkd
is a drop-in replacement for the upstream Binkd daemon. It reads the same
configuration files, uses the same BSO spool, accepts the supported Binkd command-line
options, and keeps the
.B binkd
protocol identity.
.PP
The supported platforms are Linux, macOS, and Windows NT and later. BSD is
build-supported but is not tested in CI. The upstream C implementation
remains the build for OS/2, DOS, Amiga, and Windows 9x/Me.
.PP
The executable is
.BR rbinkd .
Runtime names remain compatible: the configuration files accept the
.B rbinkd.conf
and
.B binkd.conf
names on UNIX, and the
.B rbinkd.cfg
and
.B binkd.cfg
names on Windows. The Windows service name defaults to
.BR rbinkd-service .
The legacy
.B binkd-service
name is available with
.BR "\-S binkd-service" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-a " ip"
Assume the remote address for the
.B \-i
session.
.TP
.BI \-C
Reload the configuration when the file changes.
.TP
.BI \-c
Run the client only. The default runs both the server and the client.
.TP
.BI \-D
Run as a daemon. This option is not valid in client-only mode.
.TP
.BI \-d
Dump the parsed configuration and exit.
.TP
.BI \-f " node"
Run a protected server session with this node.
.TP
.BI \-i
Run one server session on standard input and output.
.TP
.BI \-m
Disable CRAM-MD5 authorization. Implies
.BR \-r .
.TP
.BI \-n
Check the configuration and create polls without starting the managers.
.TP
.BI \-P " node"
Poll a node.
.TP
.BI \-p
Run the client manager, process polls, and quit when the queue stays empty.
Implies
.BR \-c .
.TP
.BI \-q
Be quiet.
.TP
.BI \-r
Disable crypt traffic.
.TP
.BI \-s
Run the server only.
.TP
.BI \-v
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-vv
Print the version and the build flags and exit.
.TP
.BI \-h
Print the help text and exit.
.TP
.BI \-t " command"
Run a Windows service command:
.IR install ,
.IR uninstall ,
.IR start ,
.IR stop ,
.IR restart ,
or
.IR status .
This option is available on Windows only.
.TP
.BI \-S " name"
Set the Windows service name. The default is
.BR rbinkd-service .
This option is available on Windows only.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the configuration.
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Stop the daemon after the current work is finished or aborted.
.TP
.B SIGINT
Stop the daemon.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I rbinkd.conf
The new UNIX configuration file.
.TP
.I binkd.conf
The legacy UNIX configuration file.
.TP
.I rbinkd.cfg
The new Windows configuration file.
.TP
.I binkd.cfg
The legacy Windows configuration file.
.PP
If the config argument is omitted, rbinkd checks the new name first, then
the legacy name.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RBINKD_LOG
The text log path when the config has no
.B log
directive. It takes precedence over
.BR BINKD_LOG .
.TP
.B BINKD_LOG
The legacy text log path when the config has no
.B log
directive.
.SH LIMITATIONS
ASO (Amiga-style outbound) is not implemented. The dynamic zlib and bzip2
loader keywords are not implemented.
.PP
The Windows build has no tray icon and no
.B \-T
switch. It rejects
.B syslog
and
.BR aso .
.SH SEE ALSO
The documentation index is in
.I doc/README.md
of the source tree.
.PP
The upstream Binkd project is at
.UR https://github.com/pgul/binkd
.UE .
.SH AUTHORS
The Binkd authors and the rbinkd contributors.
